<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Le Morne des Sauteurs</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1651">1651</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Caribs' Leap, Leapers' Hill</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Le Morne des Sauteurs ('Leapers' Hill'), also called Caribs' Leap, is a cliff at Sauteurs on the northern coast of Grenada. According to French accounts, in 1651 the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalinago">Kalinago</a> (Carib) defenders resisting the French colonists leapt from it to their deaths rather than surrender. The site is a national memorial, and the town of Sauteurs takes its name from the event.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/le-morne-des-sauteurs.jpg" alt="Le Morne des Sauteurs" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Agostino Brunias (1728 - 1796) – Artist (Italian, active in Britain (1758-1770; 1777-1780s)) Details on Google Art Pr... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Agostino_Brunias_-_A_Leeward_Islands_Carib_family_outside_a_Hut_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
